@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Fixed a number of operations not being safe to cancel on the asyncio backend: resources
+acquired by a cancelled operation (such as the socket connected by ``connect_tcp()``,
+files opened by ``open_file()`` or temporary files and directories) are now released,
+``aclose()`` and similar cleanup operations now complete their cleanup even when the
+calling task has been cancelled, streams left in an inconsistent state by a cancelled
+operation (TLS streams, UNIX socket streams and stateful text encoders) now raise
+``BrokenResourceError`` on further use, abandoned worker threads keep holding their
+capacity limiter token until they finish, and cancelling a ``concurrent.futures.Future``
+returned by a blocking portal no longer risks crashing the portal
